 "text": "The clause is enforceable. It gives the tenant an option and does not require the tenant to pay by post-dated cheque or pre-authorized debit. Section 106 of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006* restricts a landlord from requiring those payment methods, so a term that leaves the choice with the tenant is consistent with the Act. Section 3 also means a lease cannot waive tenant rights under the Act, but this clause does not attempt to do that.\n\nI'm working from memory of the Act's numbering, so please confirm the section against the current consolidation on e-Laws before relying on it.\n\nVerdict: enforceable\nSection: 106",
